<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50706" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be a horseman</i> or <i>rider, ride</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.136
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. ταῖς κυούσαις ἵπποις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					576a21
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. ἐπ᾽ ὄνου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Bacch.</u>
					2
				</span></i>
			; of a people, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππεύει ταῦτα τὰ ἔθνη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					7.84
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				87
			</span></i>:—also in 
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				1.27
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				79
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> metaph., of
			the wind, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζεφύρου πνοαῖς ἱππεύσαντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					212
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σελάνα ἱππεύουσα δι᾽ ὀρφναίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					994
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); also, <i>rush</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς φόνον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>HF</u>
					1001
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>serve in the cavalry</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				14.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.1.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				756b
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> at Rome,
				<i>to be an eques</i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.12
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ -εῦον</span> the <i>ordo
				equester</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				60.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> of a horse,
			as we say 'the horse <i>rides</i> (i.e. <i>carries his
			rider</i>) well', <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1.6
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>drive</i> a team, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1406
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
